WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.502
[music playing]

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.170
SMUGGLER: Boston
is the University

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:07.774
capital of the United States.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:11.010
There was a lot of rich kids
who just wanted to smoke pot.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.713
And it was the
perfect market for us.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.248
We felt indestructible.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.416
People were getting high.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.550
They loved our product.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:20.754
[music playing]

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:26.393
Our business grew and
became successful.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:31.064
We had this big pile of
cash, plenty of women.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.999
And we were just having a blast.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.568
[laughing]

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:40.473
And then one night, I
met this Colombian guy.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:46.012
And he told me there's someone
I should meet in Columbia.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.614
This guy in Columbia--

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.450
He runs an
organization, a cartel.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:55.388
SMUGGLER: --that grows 50
tons of marijuana a year,

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:59.592
and we call him el
Padrino, the godfather.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.760
He knows you.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:01.828
He wants to meet you.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.798
[music playing]

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.466
I was 20 years old.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:10.236
And some godfather in
Colombia had heard about me.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:13.573
And they wanted me to go
to Colombia to meet them.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.308
That got me excited.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.377
This was a big opportunity.

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:20.814
Columbia was known to have
top quality marijuana.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.018
And here was my chance to
get right to the source.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:28.488
It was dangerous and
breathtaking and scary.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:32.492
But the thing is I'm
a high risk junkie.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:36.563
I need to always push
things to the limit

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:40.099
to build something and keep
building it and building it

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.201
until it blew up.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.737
[music playing]

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:53.346
So the next morning I
was in a private plane,

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:57.484
flying into northern Colombia
to meet the Godfather.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:03.223
And he says, come on in.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:07.193
He looked like someone
who was deadly serious,

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.163
the mysterious hard
wired kind of person.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.633
[music playing]

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.637
The feeling that I had
was a feeling of distrust.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.642
I'm not sure what's
going on here.

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:24.477
I'm out of my element.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.151
We get about 10
miles down the road.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:37.223
And we get to a
military checkpoint.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.692
The godfather handed me the bag.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:43.963
What's this?

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.698
SMUGGLER: And I open the bag.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:49.869
And I see 50,000 pesos.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:50.870
And I see it evolving.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:57.877
And he says to me,
I want you to offer

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:00.346
the guard the pesos first.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:04.717
And if he doesn't take it,
I want you to shoot him.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:12.225
What have I got myself into?

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:15.728
Then I realize, this is a test.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:20.199
They wanna know if I
got the balls to go out

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:23.202
there and actually shoot
someone in the head who

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.504
doesn't take a bribe.

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:31.044
[music playing]

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.145
So I had no choice.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:35.548
[music playing]

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.052
I had the money and the gun.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:42.455
[music playing]

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.260
There were so many thoughts
going through my head.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.428
I hate violence.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.163
I've always hated violence.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.231
And I didn't want to shoot him.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:04:00.573
So I really hoped that
he would take that money.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:06.446
The guy looked at me.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.414
I looked at him.

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:14.520
I take a deep breath and
hand him the bag of money.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.492
[bird chirping]

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:24.831
[music playing]

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:35.808
I could tell that
he was bewildered.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.778
I needed him to take that money.

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:44.083
He looked at me and slowly
walked back towards the God

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.721
house with the bag.

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:52.125
I thought, thank God.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:55.528
And then I walked back.

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:57.497
And he asked, is everything OK?

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.936
And I said yes.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:08.041
Going on that journey was--

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.743
that was the test, right.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.981
He's challenging me to see
who's the craziest [bleep]

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:17.617
in the room, is it
him or is it me?

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:20.053
[music playing]

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:26.659
And as we got deeper into the
jungle, we got to a farmhouse.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:30.263
I noticed that there were
farm workers who were also

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:33.399
carrying shotguns and rifles.

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:35.168
It was clear to me
at that point in time

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:39.839
that he was running a
very serious operation.

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:42.742
And then as we
got over the hill,

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:45.278
I could see down in
the valley as far

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:48.081
as my eyes could see
the most beautiful

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.049
crop of marijuana plants.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:53.286
[music playing]

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:58.024
I'd never seen so much
marijuana in my life.

00:05:58.091 --> 00:06:00.927
This is at least 20,000 acres.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:02.628
[gasp]

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:03.996
This is unbelievable.

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:08.534
This is probably the largest
marijuana field in the world.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:11.571
The godfather explains
to me that they've

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:16.976
been growing here for 120
years and distributing

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:20.379
our crop in South America.

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:22.448
And then he got
down to business.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:25.251
The godfather
wanted to know is it

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:29.021
possible to move
mountains of marijuana

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:33.960
safely from this farm to the US.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:37.330
Their harvest is
50 tons per year.

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:40.833
And I thought, that's
a lot of cubic footage.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.568
It seems insane.

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:45.271
[laughing]

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.173
And then he said--

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.341
Come with me.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.745
He walked me to this barn.

00:06:56.082 --> 00:07:00.987
When he opened the door,
there was like floor

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:05.491
to ceiling US currency.

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:07.960
There were just hundreds
of bales of cash.

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:11.330
[music playing]

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:20.606
I just looked at that money,
and I thought, I love this guy.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:25.178
And then I fell in
love with his project.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:28.247
Then the Godfather
told me, it would

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:33.352
make me feel too rich that I
would make $10 to $13 million

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:34.320
a year.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.793
I said, perfect, I've been
doing the same [bleep]

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.895
on a very small scale.

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:45.898
But I know how this works now.

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:48.901
So I said, yes, and I'm in.

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:55.408
But then he said,
once you agree,

00:07:55.474 --> 00:07:58.744
you can't get out until
I say you're free to go.

00:08:01.881 --> 00:08:04.016
I had no idea what
kind of impact

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:05.184
that would have on my life.

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:07.486
[music playing]

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:15.361
[music playing]

